ad a bit more monica with my wrist”"]}, {"t": 6728, "time": "01:52:08", "artist": "pat_16120", "title": "L0ve Lett3rs", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://pat16120.bandcamp.com/", "search": false}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=pat_16120+L0ve+Lett3rs", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/pat16120/l0ve-lett3rs", "search": false}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/pat_16120+L0ve+Lett3rs", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=pat_16120+L0ve+Lett3rs", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/pat_16120+L0ve+Lett3rs", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=pat_16120+L0ve+Lett3rs&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“what you just heard before was love letters by pat 16120”", "Perth ambient/trance artist pat_16120 released 'L0ve Lett3rs' (2018), closely matching 'Pat 16120' / 'Love Letters'."]}, {"t": 7035, "time": "01:57:15", "artist": "Tourniquet", "title": "First Love", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Tourniquet+First+Love", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Tourniquet+First+Love", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Tourniquet+First+Love", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Tourniquet+First+Love", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Tourniquet+First+Love", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Tourniquet+First+Love", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Tourniquet+First+Love&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“i'm going to play first love by tourniquet”"]}, {"t": null, "time": "--:--:--", "artist": "Nicer Under Me", "title": "Ghoul's Pub", "conf": "low", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Nicer+Under+Me+Ghoul%27s+Pub", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Nicer+Under+Me+Ghoul%27s+Pub", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Nicer+Under+Me+Ghoul%27s+Pub", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Nicer+Under+Me+Ghoul%27s+Pub", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Nicer+Under+Me+Ghoul%27s+Pub", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Nicer+Under+Me+Ghoul%27s+Pub", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Nicer+Under+Me+Ghoul%27s+Pub&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“what you just heard was uh ghoul's pub by nicer under me”", "mentioned by the presenter but we couldn't work out when it played"]}, {"t": null, "time": "--:--:--", "artist": "Ego Seed", "title": "The Anytime Moment", "conf": "low", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Ego+Seed+The+Anytime+Moment", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Ego+Seed+The+Anytime+Moment", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Ego+Seed+The+Anytime+Moment", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Ego+Seed+The+Anytime+Moment", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Ego+Seed+The+Anytime+Moment", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Ego+Seed+The+Anytime+Moment", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Ego+Seed+The+Anytime+Moment&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“before that was a track by ego seed called the anytime moment”", "mentioned by the presenter but we couldn't work out when it played"]}], "counts": {"high": 1, "mid": 15, "low": 18}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:12:19", "end": "00:13:58", "text": "For the next two hours, I'll be taking you on a journey of wispy but playful, light, airy tunes that I've been listening to this week as spring has sprung and it feels like summer, honestly, with the weather at the moment. It's super sunny outside, super warm and yeah, I think that's the vibe for this episode. i think um the sounds i've been finding have been a bit windy a bit light a bit airy um yeah the the last track you heard was play outside by leppy leppy and the track before that was by the creek by deer park and at the top there we had soft dreams for small wings by kenai um all found on soundcloud which you might have heard a small ad play sorry if you heard that but please text in if you did and tell me how bad it was 0435 123 945 yeah super excited to take you on this wispy journey um we're gonna go into some more soft stuff um i'm gonna play a track i've been rinsing called change by anima um just to honor the the changing of the seasons you're on fbi this is deep web fm"}, {"start": "00:17:23", "end": "00:18:16", "text": "Yeah, but no. Before that? I've been rapping since I was a little boy. You were talking about when you were in Juvie, you became like a hot rapper. When I was in Juvie, I noticed that I really could have rapped once I noticed other people rapping the music. Yeah. But I always had a passion for, like, sounds. I started off wanting to play the drums. I think I told you this before, I used to go in the bathroom, flip, dirty clothes happens over, put the toilet seat down, get a pan, and I had drumsticks, and I used to, I always loved beats, I always loved music. Okay. I don't know why, just every time I see him, I do that. He'd be like"}, {"start": "00:21:28", "end": "00:21:59", "text": "Bitch. You got bitch problems. You can holler at me about it. Choosing this side or that side is not minding your business. You feel me? And that ain't even with me. That's with anything in life. You not minding your business if you in it."}, {"start": "00:28:38", "end": "00:31:36", "text": "You're listening to Deep Web on FBi Radio. I'm your host, Sarah El-Yugen, also known as Arsa. Thank you to Krishtie for letting me cover. I'll be covering the next couple of weeks, which I'm really excited about. Thank you, Hayley, for texting in. I swear I heard a song similar to this in a dream I had a while ago. very interesting you say that Hayley because I think when I was looking at music and listening to music for this episode I was in a dreamlike state um very up in the air um looking at the clouds as a as spring has sprung and brought us a lot of warmth this music has been keeping me warm as well um lots of sincerity in this music um what you just heard was uh ghoul's pub by nicer under me and then before that was a track by ego seed called the anytime moment um we had let's live life by mifu i love mifu and i love i love the title let's live life i think yeah this episode's about living life and living under the sunshine and kind of embracing the wispy um the wispy tangents that the wind takes us um when we let it i think soundcloud is a great place for that and um speaking of the changes i think we had small things that count by monica which i think is the song that hayley uh was talking about that's when she texted in um we had like yeah Gucci Mane reference in there but um somehow still um somehow really airy and um weightless at the same time even though that song is like sharp and hard I think the the remixes I've got um coming up are similar in that sense where yeah they kind of offer this kind of sparkly break um yeah just overall really warm just a theme of like playing outside in the park with your friends um bouncing around I think there's going to be lots of bouncy sounds and light reflecting everywhere in this um yeah upcoming few tracks I've got for you um I'm gonna play a song called grab my hand by window seeker I've been seeking a lot of windows and looking out windows I think um as the sun is out I want to put my phone down and I want to look outside and this song kind of yeah it reminds me of doing that"}, {"start": "00:52:45", "end": "00:56:27", "text": "You're listening to FBi Radio and you're listening to Deep Web FM at the moment. You're with Arsa aka Sarah El-Yugen covering for Krishtie. We just heard from Chukki Mamani Kondori, the last few tracks, also known as, previously known as Alicia Crampton, also making music under that moniker still I believe. The track that just played was Smile, a really old one from them. I really like the birds chirping. I feel like if you were listening in before and if you're new here, the episode theme so far has been about like feeling the wispiness of the wind in spring and feeling airy and light and like a feather. um with that uh folky track just then and the ones before we had uh thought of you e-dj edit also by chukimamani kundori and dreaming we also had um my entire body hurts by love life all the time and i introduced uh grab my hand by window seeker as well that long track that we opened with yeah I think I have a lot to say about Crampton aka Chukimama Nikundori um I really like how she navigates um kind of like the non-linear dimensions of time and space um I feel like she finds uh um really like lots of beauty in the eras and chaos of music and kind of how to um yeah like rewrite history almost um she comes from a background of um abolitionist theory and anti-coloniality um she's also queer and um yeah i think like uh being indigenous um i think she's from um aimara um yeah i think she's uh usually caught in between like these um western categories i believe it's a believe it's um native american could be wrong um but i think uh uh for those listening i think a lot of like um brown and queer folk um yeah i think we're constantly kind of um stuck in the in between of um the modern western music and like our old yeah our old like um folky style i think she does a really good job at like finding a through line between the two um yeah I think she travels through memory history um in the past and future at the same time which I think um yeah a lot of these remixes and like SoundCloud deep cuts um that's what they do for me so I think it really fit into um the episode so we're gonna we're gonna probably continue listening to a couple of tracked by her and then we'll see where the wind takes us this is deep web you're an fbi text line is 0435123945 i'd love to hear from you you're listening to chukimamani kundori this track is a remix called love you down"}, {"start": "01:05:15", "end": "01:05:36", "text": "Next up, I thought you'd have to shove it in there. Enjoy."}, {"start": "01:23:47", "end": "01:25:36", "text": "You're listening to FBi Radio. My name is Sara Elugan and you're on Deep Web FM. That was New Year by Ketterkatt. I've been loving her stuff lately. I think she's my favorite rapper at the moment. I would recommend anything by her. I don't think the rest of what I wanted to play by her works with the theme of this episode we've got going on. i kind of took a swerve with this track but i feel like it was like the flip side of the track before it which was called maybe i'm just being gang stalked by anima we had another anima track earlier change which kind of also um you know fed into the um the theme of the episode which is the changing of the season you know i guess this new year new me new season same me i think um we also had uh another flip uh with uh mecha talk and betty wap um i think it was a linked off remix but uh the user that uploaded it on soundcloud is called yb i'm not sure who's who with these soundcloud descriptions um but i'll have everything on the show page um probably at the end of the show since i'm yeah i'm playing off soundcloud and it's been of a been a bit of a mish trying to um